  "packet_sha256": "66303d554dced89c785caa19875849a31ea0808b6c4a9b5219545041038c823b",
  "state_summary": "Round 6 reports 525 observed records, 2805 eligible candidates, no pending records and no validation/test truth. Review of the supplied tables favors targeted tests of graph-specific solvent-response curvature and a few unresolved loading interactions. The latest measurements resolve the persistence of m28's late elution across loading and reject transfer of m211's 50/1 loading displacement to 10/1. Large new response errors on m13, m128 and m38 coexist with overprediction on m206 and m189. Their implications concern overall Row prediction after retraining; no distribution-wide improvement has been demonstrated.",
  "important_observations": [
    {
      "topic": "Nitrogen loading effects are strongly ratio dependent",
      "evidence": "Observed m211 at 10/1 changes from 18.13/30.88 mL at 54.3 mg to 15.66/32.11 at 162.9 mg (d119d77f545c029deace, 810b065b0b86ff8c9aae). The interval widens from 12.75 to 16.45 mL, without the approximately +20/+22 mL displacement recorded between those doses at 50/1 (35f2be5f5aa14265e8a4, 0f06772820e6693753e3). This directly narrows H_N_condition. For m90, increasing loading from 110.7 to 166.05 mg at 10/1 moves onset earlier by 6.47 mL and completion earlier by 1.93 mL (96710afeabc594baa359, c76d0420b34df595c0c9); at 5/1 completion instead moves later by 4.81 mL (855832bd4005ac7abdc6, b51b5dbcd2a38b174973). A common nitrogen loading correction remains unsupported."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Sterically flanked pyridine still develops substantial retention",
      "evidence": "The observed fixed 46 mg m141 curve is 12.49/23.49, 15.70/29.42 and 38.94/71.06 mL at 1/1, 2/1 and 10/1 (835b5f2641442576de42, 82d7243f61695e1b94cf, 7fb4f90753d40dd25be0). Its 10/1 premeasurement prediction was too early by 16.90/10.22 mL. Steric shielding of 2,6-dimethylpyridine nitrogen is a chemical consideration, but it does not establish weak retention under these measured conditions."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Alcohol transition questions are partly resolved and remain graph dependent",
      "evidence": "Observed m119 at 105.8 mg now progresses 11.83/19.31 → 20.00/31.61 → 48.00/77.09 mL over 1/1, 2/1 and 5/1 (25ffcaa2164643e082b9, 17c1bb3be086a2b6ffec, 776ee2c1e85ebde75168); the new interior prediction was relatively close. For m205 at 99 mg, 1/1 → 2/1 gives 18.27/33.28 → 27.63/51.49 (2b10c90b32f970e4b4c8, c973d4c257be9ef08216), rejecting its predicted shallow response. For m200 at 64.585 mg, pure EA gives 8.39/17.32 (6c022e06f98c0a9771b6), compared with 15.15/37.40 at 1/1 and 33.88/74.44 at 2/1. This establishes the strong-eluent boundary locally."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Naphthyl alcohol transfer was too strong",
      "evidence": "Observed m206 at 150 mg rises from 5.23/18.30 at 1/1 to 24.25/54.11 mL at 5/1 (a4fc5d66da363324e2bf, cdf40bcb3f4392f8d7d1). The rise is substantial, but the historical 5/1 prediction was too late by 22.20/20.75 mL. This weakens the transferred response amplitude, not the existence of a solvent response. Comparison with m205 changes side-chain connectivity, ring attachment and loading. The existing m206 50 mg 2/1 record is not an intermediate on the 150 mg curve."
    },
    {
      "topic": "The m28 tail persists across doses; another broad 10/1 loading grid has reduced value",
      "evidence": "Observed m28 at 10/1 gives 43.63/75.43, 39.13/81.40 and 38.78/80.88 mL at 58.4, 116.8 and 175.2 mg (db7f9ffa50eb931613f6, 351c17dfa8f46a8cb40a, 0dccaa29989ef4956786). Late elution survives halving the original loading. The lowest dose has a narrower interval, while the middle and highest doses have similar completions descriptively. At 175.2 mg, 5/1 measures 10.65/42.39 (050e2fab4b407ea058cb), so the matched 5/1 → 10/1 increase is +28.13/+38.48 mL. H_m28_response is locally resolved toward persistent retention with endpoint-specific loading differences; its mechanism and repeatability are unestablished."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Acid and conjugated-ketone continuations revise earlier extrapolation",
      "evidence": "At fixed 85 mg, observed m45 measures 6.63/9.00, 12.33/18.47, 18.73/31.98 and 39.58/65.65 mL at 1/1, 5/1, 10/1 and 20/1. New interior records 5cc67d02b8fad1c648d6 and 9409394cdc0bcfb31fbc were overpredicted, following the earlier 20/1 underprediction in b24f66ff77974f8ba6e1. Much of the measured increase occurs between 10/1 and 20/1; the sparse grid does not identify a sharp physical threshold. Observed m164 at 5/1 is 6.00/14.38 and was predicted closely (9f450a70d44f4384353f). Chalcone m165 at 20/1 is 6.22/23.00 (a7f8c888870123f3b277): compared with its 2/1 5.52/12.25, onset changes little while completion increases. The two conjugated ketones do not share one endpoint slope."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Ordinary carbonyl graphs show opposing transfer failures",
      "evidence": "Observed m38 at 100 mg changes from 9.32/20.87 at 5/1 to 31.48/58.15 at 20/1 (7b341f30a27433562690, 8f9a7ca0380c405ee685); both weak-eluent endpoints were underpredicted by about 18 mL. Observed m128 at 50 mg changes from 12.16/20.42 at 2/1 to 33.49/73.97 at 20/1 (40d5f6dbba8de32e9852, 55200f8e501a16ffa0cf), with the latter completion underpredicted by 37.94 mL. Conversely, m189 changes from 6.87/14.97 to 4.39/23.10 over 2/1 → 20/1 (f1dafc187f7b1ec15297, fd9cda2d3ab32ea2a360), rejecting a large predicted onset delay. Shared aromatic carbonyl functionality cannot determine residual direction."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Multifunctional ester response differs sharply from ordinary esters",
      "evidence": "Observed m13 at fixed 168.3 mg measures 9.04/18.17, 17.85/43.86 and 36.92/94.21 mL at 2/1, 5/1 and 10/1 (2dbfdf9c2d5defd09f7a, 5d530b2f228ed39ff952, ca467c94f14b2219503e). Its historical completion error changes from +13.95 to -37.64 mL between 2/1 and 10/1. In contrast, m16 at 44.25 mg changes only from 7.71/10.10 to 8.50/11.27 across 5/1 → 20/1 (66f42d226a5f7e934a86, 199a9e57ec9b13740002). m76 at 132.9 mg changes from 4.58/7.29 to 6.38/11.18 across 2/1 → 20/1 (40964ac3f659274451ef, 3fd8f569aaeff7edebea): modest, but larger than its nearly flat historical prediction. m13 contains two esters and a ketone; it should not be treated as an ordinary single ester."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Some prior ambiguities remain separate from new transfer errors",
      "evidence": "Observed m195 retains early onset at 2/1 and 10/1, 4.52 and 4.82 mL (e34787d652ccb3634f92, dc9e3983cd4f98689fa7), before the recorded 20/1 31.98/31.91 interval in a917c928912c74862968. Preserve that slightly reversed measurement. New haloarene anchors m157 and m149 had modest historical errors (8755c59209c36519ca2d, 7ce4a1f0c500c875df7c), reducing the immediate need for extensive heavy-halogen grids. Their different DCM plug volumes prevent attributing their contrast solely to halogen substitution."
    }
  ],
  "candidate_scientific_questions": [
    {
      "candidate_ids": ["2f72c334253bbe94a8ab", "cdcabd704ebeeeca9183"],
      "question": "Where does m128's large completion rise develop? At the measured 50 mg/DCM 300 uL setup, current predictions are 15.69/35.63 mL at 10/1 and 12.75/29.55 at 5/1. Either interior anchor can distinguish a response already developed at moderate ratio from a rise concentrated nearer 20/1. These are predictions, not evidence that either curve shape is correct."
