  "possible_model_blind_spots": [
    "Observed feedback requires graph-by-ratio-by-loading responses: m211 changes the kind of dose response with ratio, m90 completion changes dose-response direction, and m28 completion is approximately stable only over part of its tested dose range. Nearly flat current dose predictions can be appropriate locally while still missing these interactions.",
    "Single acquired weak-eluent labels can induce excessive correction at interior ratios, as demonstrated prospectively by m45. Current adaptation around m13, m128 and m38 therefore does not establish that their remaining curves are accurate.",
    "General chemical knowledge supports silica hydrogen bonding and acid/base interactions, and usually stronger elution with increasing EA. Steric access, dipole orientation, enolization, intramolecular hydrogen bonding, dissolution and adsorption-site occupancy are possible explanations, not findings from these endpoint measurements. HBA counts and TPSA alone do not establish equal silica interaction."
